<title>FRANCE: CNP sees 1996 net profit up at 1.57 billion francs.</title>
<headline>CNP sees 1996 net profit up at 1.57 billion francs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Caisse Nationale de Prevoyance (CNP), slated for privatisation, said it expected its 1996 net profit to be 1.57 billion francs against 1.48 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>In a statement it said its sales were up by nearly 19 percent to 100 billion francs.</p>
</text>
